Replace the libp2p PoC observer's privileged-RPC polling and custom HMAC batch
ingestion with independently authenticated per-actor OpenTelemetry metric
pipelines. Miner, follower, and signer Prometheus surfaces are filtered through
bounded Collector agents, assigned server-authoritative identities at isolated
central receivers, stored in Prometheus, and projected into freshness-aware
dashboard snapshots. Add bounded `blocked_on` and oldest-command-wait metrics;
federated traces remain structurally disabled pending their privacy audit.
Enrich the authenticated streams with bounded public signer identity, reward-set
weight, signer state-machine progress, and endpoint-free corroborated topology
from a server-owned enrollment registry and public Stacks APIs.
Split browser access into an explicit public-safe chain/reward-set projection
and a server-session-protected federation view. Add a PoC-only development
password provider behind an OIDC-ready principal boundary and reconstruct the
miner's single bounded latest signer quorum round for enrolled cooperating
signers without exposing transport identities or endpoints to the client.
Expose every allowlisted node and signer metric in the authenticated portal,
aggregate signer latency histograms, derive an explicitly height-only tip
adoption spread, and separate signer node-tip observation freshness from the
slower account/PoX monitoring cadence.
Project the complete enrolled-actor libp2p graph by joining each bounded current
transport PeerId against a unique server-owned enrollment. Unknown external
peers remain scalar counts, endpoints remain excluded, stale identity labels
are removed to bound lifetime cardinality, and raw PeerIds are consumed
server-side instead of entering the client metric catalogue. Distinguish
configured signer–companion service bindings from observed connectivity, use
compact in-node labels, and support actor focus isolation at the 28-actor limit.
Keep authenticated SSE streams open under normal large-snapshot backpressure by
coalescing to one latest pending snapshot and resuming on drain, instead of
mistaking a full response buffer for a disconnected viewer.
Replace newest-height-as-canonical health with largest same-height cohort
agreement, leaving newest-height coverage as a separate propagation signal.

For the maximum-scale PoC, use durable status snapshots, coherent
provider-affine IBD plans, a bounded fair metadata queue, and periodic signer
replay cursor refresh. The replay refresh repairs simultaneous-startup gaps in
which an empty early replay and a pre-mesh one-shot state publication otherwise
prevent signers from negotiating their protocol version, without lowering the
consensus threshold or relying on startup timing.
Retry signer local-state initialization after a transiently incomplete
companion-node tenure view, and publish a bounded ten-second signed state
heartbeat. Previously, an IBD-time `NoParentTenureInfo` left the signer
permanently uninitialized until process restart.
Generate role-specific PoC connection ceilings so the maximum topology remains
sparse instead of converging into a 28-actor clique: ordinary nodes and signers
retain bounded rendezvous paths plus a GossipSub mesh, while miner and bootstrap
ceilings preserve quorum reachability and recovery capacity.
Keep terminal signer-round telemetry internally consistent with the miner's
authoritative approval and explicitly zero obsolete per-signer series so a
federated Prometheus staleness window cannot resurrect an earlier decision.
Reserve signer connection capacity for configured rendezvous peers before swarm
startup, require multi-hop GossipSub evidence from at least half of a large
signer set, and bound verifier log scans. Scale the PoC miner's post-restart
block-commit delay below the flash-block floor and reject any run where a miner
falls below Nakamoto's 3-of-6 commitment rule.
